# grammar: v0 (unfrozen; AST normative)
#
# true-naming — the arbitrariness proof of 04-practices §4, completed: a practice
# whose resource is graded-monotone DECAY (nothing spent, knowing only wears),
# whose names are DIALECT-DERIVATIONS, and whose premises are KNOWLEDGE STATES.
# Three layers — magic, language, and story-time — meet in one pack, zero kernel
# code. Standing role: the workbench's acceptance test (04 §4).
scope magic

use language          # true-naming consumes the language layer wholesale
use chronology        # ...and story-time, for the knowledge states

# --- dialect-derived names: a true-name IS a dialect derivation (05 §2) ------
dialect fen-tongue "the fen tongue"  proposed {
  vowels a e i o u y
  endings -a -en -eth
  cluster-max 2
  stress penultimate
  name-kind person.given = given-proto given-deutero
  name-part sae "still-water"      role given-proto    proposed
  name-part wen "one-who-tends"    role given-deutero  proposed
  }

name saewen "Saewen"  person.given in fen-tongue
  = given-proto sae + given-deutero wen
  bearer the-marsh-child   proposed
  # checked at compile: slot sequence matches a name-kind pattern, each name-part
  # exists under its claimed role, the composed form passes the phonotactics.
  # A mispronunciation is literally a dialect-derivation failure (L4 below).

# --- knowledge states: knowing a name is a fact with a validity span ----------
event the-naming-day   during the-beleaguered-present   proposed
state knows.caster.saewen = true  since the-naming-day   proposed
# learning a name is a knowledge state initiated when it is learned;
# query knows(caster, true-name(bearer)) as-of a scene (03-time §4).

# --- the practice: graded-monotone decay (04 §4) ------------------------------
practice true-naming  proposed {
  use language.registers                # its primitives ARE the naming layer
  resource acquaintance(name) : graded monotone whole > worn > husk
  rule invoke(bearer) requires
      knows(caster, true-name(bearer)),
      acquaintance(true-name(bearer)) >= worn,
      derivation(true-name(bearer)) checks in register-of(bearer)
  effect invoke degrades acquaintance by 1     # speaking a name wears it
  condition unheard requires no witness within earshot
  error slipped-name   refines L4 bad-instantiation
                       # a mispronunciation IS a failed dialect derivation
  error stale-name     refines L2 where premise-outdated
                       # the bearer has changed since the name was learned
  error name-overheard refines L3 side-condition [unheard] signals degrade(+1)
  cost social | epistemic
  }

# --- the craft the practice serves, and the open fork it leaves ---------------
rule show-the-cost over season  proposed
principle name-earns-its-weight  proposed

fork what-does-a-name-cost
  option a-memory
  option a-year-of-service

# Disjointness ledger (04 §4): the one honest cost this fixture exacts is adding
# `graded monotone` to the resource algebra. Had it needed a second new algebra
# member, the parameterization would have failed — which is what makes the
# fixture load-bearing. Nothing here resembles proof-magic's conserved debt.
